Yes, your understanding is correct. The lock status will be stored centrally in the database so that all PPI Tracker users can check whether a cell or entity is currently being edited.  

The lock information will be stored separately from the actual tracker data as temporary lock records. Each record will identify the project, target cell or entity, user who started editing, a secure lock token, and an expiry time.  

For direct “Edit in Cell,” the system will store a lock for the specific cell. For the full Edit Entity dialog, the system will store a lock for the selected entity. When multiple entities are edited together, the system will store locks for all selected entities as one batch.  

The lock will be removed when the user saves, cancels, or closes the editor. If the application closes unexpectedly, the lock will expire automatically after a short period. While the user is editing, the application will renew the lock periodically.  

In addition, the system will check the latest data revision when saving, as a safeguard against accidental overwrites.  

